I don't get your issue here.  Is it annoying because you failed
to get to the same score as a prior game with the same name,
class, species, sex and alignment?  If you change any of
those initial values it displays them in the top 10.  If you don't
then you're playing the same combination again and again.

When playing the same combination again and again all that
really matters is if you survived longer than any of your previous
games.  (High score matters before ascending, low score
matters among ascensions.  Wierd.)  What's annoying is not
progressing as it means there's some skill issue you're missing.
What's not annoying is the score.

For example for a long time I played lawful human female valk
after lawful human female valk.  Each game either I died early
and the score didn't matter, or I advanced my skills a bit and
I survived farther into the game so my score did matter.  Then
for a long time I played chaotic human male wizard after chaotic
human male wizard.  Same deal but it was a lot of games before
I learned the style of spellcasting players to beat my better vlak
games.  Then I moved on to playing some other class.  When I
started playing random players that's when a lot of characters
shuffled in the top 10 display.

So to me the issue isn't what's displayed - The issue is you're
playing the same class again and again and not advancing.
That means you're missing out on some skill issue to help you
advance your game.  Frustrating indeed, but that's why Nethack
remains interesting after so long.


